details.image_prompt:
[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features two simple, matte ceramic bowls set on an aged, dark oak wood tabletop. The composition is a 3/4 overhead angle, perfectly capturing the contents of both bowls with a shallow depth of field, keeping the front bowl in sharp focus while the second is softly blurred in the background. Soft, natural light streams from a window on the left, casting gentle shadows and highlighting the glistening balsamic-coated ingredients. In each bowl, a base of fresh, vibrant baby arugula is tossed with halved, glossy cherry tomatoes and tender, halved artichoke hearts. A generous, warm serving of nutty, golden-brown farro is spooned over the salad base, with seared, caramelized sirloin steak strips placed neatly alongside the farro, not stacked, revealing their dark, crusty edges and succulent, tender centers. A slight, dark balsamic glaze shimmer clings to the tomatoes and greens. Props include a single wooden fork resting casually on the wood surface, a small, slightly messy spill of a few farro grains near the bowl, and a stray arugula leaf on the table. The image radiates a warm, inviting, lived-in aesthetic. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating—lived-in, warm, authentic. Slight natural imperfections: an asymmetric garnish placement, a small balsamic drip on the bowl rim, slightly uneven searing on the steak. Include subtle traces of the cooking process: a few scattered farro grains on the surface, no plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces. Warm, golden-hour color temperature, cozy and inviting. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from a photograph taken by a professional food photographer for a printed cookbook."
]
